.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.Dd @NCOLLECTD_DATE@
.Dt NCOLLECTD-DOCKER 5
.Os ncollectd @NCOLLECTD_VERSION@
.Sh NAME
.Nm ncollectd-docker
.Nd Documentation of ncollectd's docker plugin
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal -compact
\fBload-plugin\fP docker
\fBplugin\fP docker {
    \fBinstance\fP \fIname\fP {
        \fBurl\fP \fIurl\fP
        \fBsocket-path\fP \fIpath\fP
        \fBca-cert\fP \fI/path/to/ca-cert\fP
        \fBclient-key\fP \fI/path/to/client-key\fP
        \fBclient-cert\fP \fI/path/to/client-cert\fP
        \fBlabel\fP \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
        \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBfilter\fP {
            ...
        }
    }
}
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The \fBdocker\fP plugin collects statistics from docker running containers.
It uses version 1.40 of the Docker Engine API (Docker 19.03 or later).
.Pp
In the \fBplugin\fP block, there may be one or more \fBinstance\fP blocks,
each defining a docker daemon.
.Pp
The following options are valid within \fBinstance\fP blocks:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \fBurl\fP \fIurl\fP
Base URL of the docker daemon API, for example \fIhttp://127.0.0.1:2375\fP
or \fIhttps://127.0.0.1:2376\fP; the API path is appended to it.
When \fBsocket-path\fP is set the connection is made through the socket.
.It \fBsocket-path\fP \fIpath\fP
Path of the UNIX socket of the docker daemon, usually
\fI/var/run/docker.sock\fP.
At least one of \fBurl\fP or \fBsocket-path\fP must be set.
.It \fBca-cert\fP \fI/path/to/ca-cert\fP
File that holds one or more SSL certificates used to verify the docker
daemon when \fBurl\fP uses HTTPS.
.It \fBclient-key\fP \fI/path/to/client-key\fP
File that holds the private key in PEM format to be used for certificate-based
authentication, as required by a docker daemon started with \fB--tlsverify\fP.
.It \fBclient-cert\fP \fI/path/to/client-cert\fP
File that holds the SSL certificate to be used for certificate-based
authentication.
.It \fBlabel\fP \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
Append the label \fIkey\fP=\fIvalue\fP to the submitting metrics.
Can appear multiple time in the \fBinstance\fP block.
.It \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
The \fBtimeout\fP option sets the overall timeout for the requests that list
the containers and the connection timeout of the statistics streams, in
seconds.
By default the collection interval is used.
.It \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
Sets the interval (in seconds) in which the values will be collected from this
instance.
By default the global \fBinterval\fP setting will be used.
.It \fBfilter\fP
Configure a filter to modify or drop the metrics.
See \fBFILTER CONFIGURATION\fP in
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5 .
.El
.Sh "SEE ALSO"
.Xr ncollectd 1 ,
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5
